cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use CarbonLens in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "CarbonLens: A Browser-Native CO2 Storage Pre-Screening Tool"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-06-17"
authors:
  - family-names: Olagunju
    given-names: Daniel T.
    affiliation: "Universiti Teknologi PETRONAS"
    orcid: ""
repository-code: "https://github.com/carbonlens/carbonlens"
abstract: >
  CarbonLens is an open-source, browser-native CO2 geological storage screening tool
  implementing peer-reviewed analytical physics (Nordbotten 2005, Hesse 2008, Span-Wagner 1996,
  Duan-Sun 2003, Duan 2006, Fenghour 1998, Land 1968, Theis 1935) with heterogeneous formation
  corrections (Shook & Mitchell 2009, Kopp et al. 2010) and a white-box MARS surrogate for
  CO2-brine interfacial tension. Designed for pre-FEED screening, education, and regulatory
  pre-application support.
keywords:
  - "CO2 storage"
  - "carbon capture and storage"
  - "geological storage"
  - "CCUS"
  - "screening tool"
license: MIT
